    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths feels like a natural way of thinking—structured yet creative. It’s both frustrating when stuck on complex problems (like my high neuroticism levels sometimes make me feel) and rewarding when patterns click. My parents’ differing educational backgrounds made me value it as a bridge between abstract ideas and concrete applications, especially in chemistry I love. It’s not just numbers but logic and problem-solving.",
